t the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta),$ the region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta):0\\leq r\\leq \\sqrt{2},\\ \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\leq\\theta\\leq \\pi\\}.\n$$\n\nSince $r\\geq0$, $\\sqrt{r^2}=r$; also $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$.\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D \\left(x^{2} - y^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}A&=\\iint_\\Delta \\left((r\\cos\\theta)^{2} - (r\\sin\\theta)^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{(r\\cos\\theta)^{2} + (r\\sin\\theta)^{2}}\\,r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^3(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\sqrt{r^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^4(\\cos^2\\theta-\\sin^2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^4\\cos(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38fd4660-39ca-585f-8e3a-5d8b569be77d" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Double Integral Over a Circle or Part-Circle Centered at the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026784b9-3bc0-5798-b8b5-2ea62f5c5f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535297} {:answer/id #uuid "0cad4500-905a-5858-8c3f-a7b60b352b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535299} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb01dae-041f-5459-8b96-b3482e964c0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535304} {:answer/id #uuid "8e67acde-888e-5817-a582-ac7742afc991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535324} {:answer/id #uuid "f8da406d-b2dc-5b56-b3c5-186cce25d980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e67acde-888e-5817-a582-ac7742afc991" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535324} :answer-field/id #uuid "11f6bfad-4fb4-53b7-b7e6-318260e0f958" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b24cc741-a0e1-52fd-84de-966d881c283d" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7bd61d778e3ea17a10adad21dd63cfae068af48700e6217194bb48e995c9f6e7.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the circle shown above. What is ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A$ expressed in polar coordinates?\n\nChoose a change-of-variables setup with $r\\geq0$ that describes $D$ and the transformed integrand, including the Jacobian." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,dA={∬}_{Δ}\\,f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,dr\\,d\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents the disk of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta):0\\leq r\\leq \\sqrt{2},\\ 0\\leq\\theta\\leq 2 \\pi\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}((r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}-(r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{r}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535332 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38fd4660-39ca-585f-8e3a-5d8b569be77d" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Double Integral Over a Circle or Part-Circle Centered at the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49babc88-c8f0-56cc-8e02-d30ec1d26157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535311} {:answer/id #uuid "67e550be-2618-51a5-b473-ae78444d24d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\frac{3 \\pi}{4}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535319} {:answer/id #uuid "74e8cc33-262d-54d0-9d13-a5424bcf12e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535322} {:answer/id #uuid "9424c60b-ac35-5ce4-87fb-8d2efb4c4191" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{5} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535325} {:answer/id #uuid "def0eed0-b0f4-542a-9f44-1d63a9047258" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{3} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49babc88-c8f0-56cc-8e02-d30ec1d26157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\sin{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535311} :answer-field/id #uuid "f466e166-f8a5-5be5-ab7f-55508e3ed84a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "be642d90-5a10-50aa-88ca-50cea7daf117" :question/problem "![](images/66/66c8e80f89c7964cae5443f9e3cb04916ec6aee3e16f27480d8d85d3a344187e.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is the quarter-circle shown above. What is $\\iint_D 2 x y \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}A$ expressed in polar coordinates?\n\nChoose a change-of-variables setup with $r\\geq0$ that describes $D$ and the transformed integrand, including the Jacobian." :question/worked-solution "We will use the change of variables formula in the form\n\n$$\n\\iint_D f(x,y)\\,\\mathrm{d}A=\\iint_\\Delta f(r\\cos\\theta,r\\sin\\theta)\\,r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta.\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the region $D$ represents a portion of the disk of radius $\\sqrt{2}$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta),$ the region can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\Delta=\\{(r,\\theta):0\\leq r\\leq \\sqrt{2},\\ \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\leq\\theta\\leq \\pi\\}.\n$$\n\nSince $r\\geq0$, $\\sqrt{r^2}=r$; also $\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta=1$.\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\iint_D 2 x y \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}A&=\\iint_\\Delta 2 (r\\cos\\theta) (r\\sin\\theta) \\sqrt{(r\\cos\\theta)^{2} + (r\\sin\\theta)^{2}}\\,r\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}2r^3\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta\\sqrt{r^2(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}2r^4\\cos\\theta\\sin\\theta\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta \\\\ &=\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}^{\\pi}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^4\\sin(2\\theta)\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535337 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38fd4660-39ca-585f-8e3a-5d8b569be77d" :knowledge-point/title "Rewriting a Double Integral Over a Circle or Part-Circle Centered at the Origin"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "006f8cc3-fe44-506e-abc5-5bcc0cdda89d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{2 \\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535296} {:answer/id #uuid "3b07f7ba-836e-561a-b89e-43ec179cff33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{3} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535307} {:answer/id #uuid "41705678-4952-599d-819d-ab0c479baa66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535309} {:answer/id #uuid "c81d2b5f-e76b-538a-a273-bbf8662e4bad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}r^{4} \\cos{\\left(2 \\theta \\right)}\\,\\mathrm{d}r\\,\\mathrm{d}\\theta" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535333} {:answer/id #uuid "d42cb897-fc52-56c1-aaa4-b8bdafde567b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :a